From: pixel2 ubuntu port
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: venc: make every I-frame an IDR

venc sets HFI_PROPERTY_CONFIG_VENC_IDR_PERIOD to 0, "only the first
I-frame is IDR". The periodic keyframes (every gop_size frames) are then
non-IDR I-frames. The encoder flags them V4L2_BUF_FLAG_KEYFRAME and a
muxer writes them as sync samples, but a decoder cannot start there: an
H.264 MP4 from v4l2h264enc decodes front to back (300/300 frames on
macOS), while seeking to any point after the first GOP fails with
"Cannot Decode" (pixel2 tests 64-65; HEVC was not affected).

Use 1, every I-frame an IDR, so each keyframe is a random-access point.

---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -766,7 +766,13 @@
 		 * n > 1 - every n-th I-frame will be IDR frame
 		 */
 		ptype = HFI_PROPERTY_CONFIG_VENC_IDR_PERIOD;
-		idrp.idr_period = 0;
+		/*
+		 * Every I-frame an IDR: with 0 the periodic keyframes are
+		 * non-IDR I-frames that a muxer still marks as sync samples,
+		 * and players cannot start decoding there (seeking in an
+		 * MP4 fails until the next IDR, i.e. never).
+		 */
+		idrp.idr_period = 1;
 		ret = hfi_session_set_property(inst, ptype, &idrp);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
